e real and imaginary parts are multiplied.","The number is replaced by $0_{\\mathbb{C}}$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c9fc135c1274c719d8fc186f"},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_complex_conjugate_f5b692eb_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $\\overline{1+\\mathrm{i}}$?","options":["$-1+\\mathrm{i}$","$1+\\mathrm{i}$","$-1-\\mathrm{i}$","$1-\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7532990589e9e042c17b3923"},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_complex_conjugate_f5b692eb_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $\\overline{-2-3\\mathrm{i}}$?","options":["$2-3\\mathrm{i}$","$2+3\\mathrm{i}$","$-2+3\\mathrm{i}$","$-2-3\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3344ca7b0cb3fd5020997f23"},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_complex_conjugate_f5b692eb_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which identity about conjugates of sums is true?","options":["$\\overline{z+w} = \\overline z-\\overline w$","$\\overline{z+w} = \\overline z+\\overline w$","$\\overline{z+w} = z+w$","$\\overline{z+w} = 0_{\\mathbb{C}}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"630d024887fcfb52218f4a49"},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_complex_conjugate_f5b692eb_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Geometrically, how are $z$ and $\\overline z$ related in the complex plane?","options":["They are symmetric about the imaginary axis.","They always lie on the same vertical line with identical imaginary parts.","They are symmetric about the real axis.","They always coincide only when the real part is zero."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"deb50a58595b5f850438df69"},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_complex_conjugate_f5b692eb_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $z = 3-4\\mathrm{i}$ and $w = 1+2\\mathrm{i}$, what is $\\overline z+\\overline w$?","options":["$4-2\\mathrm{i}$","$2+6\\mathrm{i}$","$3+8\\mathrm{i}$","$4+2\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"85e3bb19e902eaca1cdc0df9"},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_complex_conjugate_f5b692eb_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $z = 2+5\\mathrm{i}$. What is $-\\overline z$?","options":["$-2-5\\mathrm{i}$","$2-5\\mathrm{i}$","$-2+5\\mathrm{i}$","$2+5\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"062450f25660b2ccdc865f8b"},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_complex_conjugate_f5b692eb_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which equation holds exactly when $z$ is real (that is, $z=a+0\\mathrm{i}$)?","options":["$\\overline z = z$","$\\overline z = -z$ for every such $z$","$z$ is symmetric about the imaginary axis with $\\overline z$","$\\overline z$ has real part $0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"962a9a15ba73a00b469bf789"},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_complex_conjugate_f5b692eb_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which identity from the definition connects conjugation with multiplication?","options":["$\\overline{zw} = z+\\overline w$","$\\overline{zw} = \\overline z-\\overline w$","$\\overline{zw} = 0_{\\mathbb{C}}$ for all $z,w$","$\\overline{zw} = \\overline z\\cdot\\overline w$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f6cdae20a963dacab4003b2d"},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_complex_conjugate_f5b692eb_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Let $z = 1+2\\mathrm{i}$ and $w = 3-\\mathrm{i}$. Using the stated property, what is $\\overline{z+w}$?","options":["$4-\\mathrm{i}$","$4+\\mathrm{i}$","$2-3\\mathrm{i}$","$-4+\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ff0caefff2445543ed682aea"},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_complex_conjugate_f5b692eb_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"L